msgstr "تحويل {translatedUnits} وأكثر."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:179
msgid "Convert acres to hectares for farmland, conservation land, and solar-farm footprints when US acreage must match metric agricultural stats. One hectare is 10,000 m²; one acre is 4,046.8564224 m², so 1 acre ≈ 0.404686 ha."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:221
msgid "Convert acres to square metres when a US land deed in acres must feed metric civil engineering, drainage calculations, or EU-style planning apps. One acre is exactly 4,046.8564224 m². Surveyors and solar designers use this for panel layout density."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:321
msgid "Convert avoirdupois ounces to grams for metric baking, lab sample limits, and nutrition labels when the US package speaks in ounces. Multiply oz by 28.349523125. Letter mail and spice jars often need grams for customs forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:309
msgid "Convert avoirdupois pounds to kilograms for passport medical forms, EU shipping labels, and metric gym programs when the starting number is in pounds. Multiply lb by 0.45359237 exactly. Couriers and coaches use this daily."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:345
msgid "Convert avoirdupois pounds to metric tonnes for export documents, port tariffs, and metric axle-load rules when the weighbridge ticket is in pounds. Divide lb by about 2,204.62. Containerized cargo filings often need tonnes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2440
msgid "Convert between running pace (minutes per kilometre) and speed in km/h or mph, set treadmills correctly, and compare race paces across metric and US displays."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1536
msgid "Convert body weight, luggage, and grocery labels between kilograms and pounds with exact factors, mental shortcuts, and habits that prevent airport and gym mistakes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2140
msgid "Convert British stone and pounds to kilograms and pounds, read UK body-weight phrases correctly, and avoid decimal-stone mistakes on forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:129
msgid "Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit for cooking, weather apps, and HVAC setpoints when a recipe or forecast is metric but your oven or thermostat shows °F. Travelers and home bakers cross this daily. Use °F = °C × 9/5 + 32, not a simple scale factor."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:141
msgid "Convert Celsius to Kelvin for science, gas laws, and color-temperature adjacent physics where absolute temperature is required. Chemistry labs and meteorology (potential temperature) use Kelvin. Add 273.15; the degree size matches Celsius."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:265
msgid "Convert cubic feet to litres for fridge interiors, grow-tent volumes, and compressed-air receiver sizing when US appliance specs meet metric lab or aquarium gear. One cubic foot is about 28.3168 L."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:235
msgid "Convert cubic metres to litres for bottled-water equivalents, fish stocking guides, and pump capacity when the engineering drawing uses m³. Multiply m³ by 1,000. Municipal water reports often flip between these for public communication."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:253
msgid "Convert cups to millilitres when baking and cooking across US/metric recipes. Cup sizes vary by country; this tool’s Cup unit maps to its configured cup definition—check which cup your recipe assumes (US legal cup is 240 mL; many metric recipes use 250 mL)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:463
msgid "Convert days to hours for shipping ETAs, antibiotic courses, and server uptime when plans use days but operations think in hours. Multiply days by 24 for civil mean days. Logistics and on-call rotations rely on this."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:493
msgid "Convert days to Julian years when mission elapsed time, fossil age approximations, or simulation ticks in days should become year-scale figures using 365.25 d/yr. Divide days by 365.25. Astrophysics notebooks use this for tidy axes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:481
msgid "Convert days to weeks for long training blocks, visa stays, and content calendars when a day count must become week language. Divide days by 7. Athletes periodizing plans and PMs phasing releases use this."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:135
msgid "Convert Fahrenheit to Celsius for European recipes, lab protocols, and weather comparisons when the source is US customary. Fever checks and pool heaters also flip between scales. Use °C = (°F − 32) × 5/9."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:153
msgid "Convert Fahrenheit to Kelvin when US process specs (°F) feed equations that need absolute temperature—ideal gas work, thermal noise, or materials science. Convert °F→°C first, then add 273.15, or use K = (°F + 459.67) × 5/9."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:407
msgid "Convert feet per second to mph when a US lab, wind-tunnel, or projectile chronograph reads ft/s but you want road-speed intuition. Divide ft/s by 1.46667, or use mph = ft/s × 15/22. Safety briefings often want mph."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:79
msgid "Convert feet to centimetres for height charts, ski length, and doorway clearances when the measurement started on a US tape in feet and inches. Medical growth charts outside the US and online clothing filters often want centimetres. Multiply feet by 30.48."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:103
msgid "Convert feet to inches when cut lists, sewing patterns, or height forms ask for a single inch total instead of feet-and-inches. Cabinetry screws, pipe runs, and printer paper clearance checks often need one number. Multiply feet by 12."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:315
msgid "Convert grams to avoirdupois ounces for coffee beans, mailers, and recipe scaling when kitchen scales show grams but US packaging lists ounces. One ounce is exactly 28.349523125 g. Portion control and postage brackets use this scale."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:351
msgid "Convert grams to kilograms for shopping, lab reagents, and postage when fine scales use grams but tariffs and recipes batch in kilograms. Divide grams by 1,000. Food service and compounding pharmacies jump this scale often."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:369
msgid "Convert grams to milligrams when a lab balance reading in grams must match pharmaceutical or supplement labels in mg. Multiply grams by 1,000. Compounding and nutrition science use this constantly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:185
msgid "Convert hectares to acres when metric land registries, vineyard sizes, or park plans must be explained to an audience that uses acres. Multiply hectares by about 2.47105. Forestry and agronomy papers often need this for US readers."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:289
msgid "Convert hectolitres to litres for brewery output, wine harvest tanks, and agricultural liquid fertilizer when industry quotes hL but cellar or field gear is labeled in L. Multiply hL by 100. European beer statistics are often in hectolitres."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:469
msgid "Convert hours to days for project timelines, drug half-life discussions, and SLA windows when engineering logs hours but managers want days. Divide hours by 24. Incident postmortems often make this switch for readability."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:451
msgid "Convert hours to minutes for parking tickets, roasting schedules, and billing increments when the quote is in hours but the clock works in minutes. Multiply hours by 60. Salons, ovens, and consultants use this constantly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:499
msgid "Convert hours to seconds for computation timeouts, video timecode budgets, and physics problems that need SI seconds from a human hour count. Multiply hours by 3,600. Software and lab DAQ systems prefer seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:25
msgid "Convert inches to centimetres when a US tape measure, pipe schedule, or monitor size must match metric drawings, European furniture specs, or metric drill bits. Builders working from mixed plans and anyone ordering parts across regions use this constantly. The international inch is locked at 25.4 mm, so the centimetre result is exact."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:43
msgid "Convert inches to millimetres when a US fractional drill size, sheet-metal gauge note, or 3D-print dimension must land on a metric CNC program or European fastener chart. Machinists and makers do this whenever CAM software expects mm. Multiply inches by 25.4 for an exact millimetre value."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1675
msgid "Convert into the unit the carrier’s rate card uses for chargeable weight, then compare actual and dimensional weight in that same unit."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:487
msgid "Convert Julian years to days for astronomy, orbital periods, and light-travel teaching when a Julian year (exactly 365.25 days) is the definition in play. This matches the year length used in the light-year definition. Science writing prefers Julian years over vague “calendar years” for long spans."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:147
msgid "Convert Kelvin to Celsius when a datasheet, blackbody formula, or cryogenics note lists K but you need everyday Celsius for baths, freezers, or weather context. Subtract 273.15. Space and semiconductor docs often stay in K until the last step."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:159
msgid "Convert Kelvin to Fahrenheit for US engineering reviews when research papers quote absolute temperature but shop-floor instruments read °F. Aerospace and HVAC commissioning sometimes need this bridge. Use °F = K × 9/5 − 459.67."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:303
msgid "Convert kilograms to avoirdupois pounds for body weight, luggage, and gym plates when scales or airlines mix SI and US customary units. Shipping rate cards and protein powder tubs cross this pair constantly. One kilogram is about 2.20462 lb."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:357
msgid "Convert kilograms to grams for baking percentages, supplement scoops, and chemistry stock solutions when the bulk bag is in kg but the formula lists grams. Multiply kg by 1,000. Baker’s percentages become easier in grams."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:327
msgid "Convert kilograms to stone for body weight in the UK and Ireland, where stone remains common in conversation and some medical contexts. One stone is 14 avoirdupois pounds, exactly 6.35029318 kg. Athletes and clinics still quote stone and pounds together."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:61
msgid "Convert kilometres to miles for road trips, race results, and fuel economy discussions when maps or cars show km but drivers think in miles. Tourism, logistics, and running (5K, 10K) all cross this boundary. One international mile is exactly 1.609344 km."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:419
msgid "Convert km/h to knots when metric weather apps must match nautical instruments, sailing polars, or aviation METAR-style expectations. Divide km/h by 1.852. Harbor masters and student pilots do this when switching unit systems."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:395
msgid "Convert km/h to m/s for drag equations, ballistic apps, and lab write-ups that need SI base units. Divide km/h by 3.6. Engineering fluid notes and school physics prefer m/s."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:377
msgid "Convert km/h to mph for road speed limits, car dashboards, and running pace talk when traveling between metric and US/UK customary roads. Divide km/h by 1.609344. Rental cars and GPS unit settings drive this daily."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:413
msgid "Convert knots to km/h for marine and aviation contexts when instruments show knots but coastal forecasts or metric pilots want km/h. One knot is one nautical mile per hour = 1.852 km/h exactly. Charts and AIS traffic use knots; phones often show km/h."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2215
msgid "Convert knots, miles per hour, kilometres per hour, and metres per second for aviation and meteorology—without confusing airspeed types or nautical vs statute miles."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:121
msgid "Convert light-years to kilometres when popular science distances (nearby stars, galaxy separations) must become a terrestrial kilometre scale for comparison or calculation. Planetarium scripts and astronomy outreach use this pair. One Julian light-year is about 9.4607×10¹² km."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:271
msgid "Convert litres to cubic feet when metric cooler, tank, or heater capacities must match US appliance and HVAC catalog language. Divide litres by about 28.3168. Importers localizing EU product sheets use this pair."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:229
msgid "Convert litres to cubic metres for water tanks, aquarium sums, and HVAC airflow-adjacent liquid volumes when SI building models want m³. One cubic metre is exactly 1,000 L. Civil and aquarium hobby math share this pair."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:295
msgid "Convert litres to hectolitres for brewery KPIs, dairy intakes, and bulk wine contracts that report in hL. Divide litres by 100. Trade statistics and cooperative milk collections often prefer hectolitres."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:247
msgid "Convert litres to millilitres when a metric recipe, IV bag scale, or fuel additive dose starts in litres but syringes and measuring cups read mL. Multiply litres by 1,000. Clinical and culinary workflows both need this."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:425
msgid "Convert m/s to mph when SI sensor logs, drone telemetry, or physics results must be explained in US customary road units. Multiply m/s by about 2.23694. Research papers often leave speed in m/s until the public summary."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:389
msgid "Convert metres per second to kilometres per hour for weather winds, physics problems, and athletics when SI base speed must become everyday road units. Multiply m/s by 3.6 exactly. Meteorology and school labs share this pair."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:49
msgid "Convert metres to feet for room dimensions, athletic track splits, and building heights when the source is metric but the audience thinks in feet. Architects reviewing SI drawings for a US client and runners comparing race distances use this pair often. One metre is about 3.28084 international feet."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:97
msgid "Convert metres to kilometres for race distances, hiking elevation gain written in metres of trail length, and city planning where short SI lengths become map-scale distances. Sensors and GPS traces often store metres; reports prefer kilometres. Divide metres by 1,000."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:85
msgid "Convert metres to yards for American football field talk, fabric bolts, and gardening beds when the plan is metric but the store sells by the yard. Landscapers and sports fans cross this pair often. One metre is about 1.09361 international yards."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:277
msgid "Convert metric tablespoons to teaspoons when scaling dressings, baking powder, and medicine-style kitchen doses. In the metric set used here, 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons (15 mL vs 5 mL). Recipe scaling and substitution both need this."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:283
msgid "Convert metric teaspoons to tablespoons to simplify long spoon counts in cooking and home remedies. Divide teaspoons by 3 when using the metric 5 mL / 15 mL pair. Cake recipes with many small leavening doses benefit from consolidating to tablespoons."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:339
msgid "Convert metric tonnes to avoirdupois pounds for freight, scrap metal, and agricultural loads when SI shipping weight must meet US scale tickets. One tonne is 1,000 kg ≈ 2,204.62 lb. Logistics brokers quote both constantly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1686
msgid "Convert miles per hour and kilometres per hour for foreign road signs, rental cars, and trip planning—plus the distance and time links that keep ETA math honest."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:67
msgid "Convert miles to kilometres when US highway distances, flight route charts in statute miles, or bike computer settings must match metric signage and European navigation. Couriers quoting door-to-door miles for overseas clients need the km figure. Multiply miles by 1.609344."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:363
msgid "Convert milligrams to grams for medicine, caffeine content, and analytical chemistry when labels use mg but balances or protocols use grams. Divide mg by 1,000. Pharmacy math depends on this shift."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:241
msgid "Convert millilitres (named Millimetre in this volume set) to litres for medicine cups, cocktail jiggers, and lab aliquots when labels use mL but dosing math wants litres. Divide millilitres by 1,000. Pharmacies and home brewing share this scale jump."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:259
msgid "Convert millilitres to cups when a European recipe lists mL but your scoop set is cups only. Divide by your cup size (often 240 or 250 mL). Home bakers scaling drink and batter volumes use this daily."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:457
msgid "Convert minutes to hours for payroll, flight duration summaries, and battery-life claims when the raw timer is in minutes. Divide minutes by 60. Timesheets and travel itineraries prefer fractional or HH:MM hours."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:439
msgid "Convert minutes to seconds for workout intervals, exposure times, and PLC timers when coaches or cameras speak in minutes but devices count seconds. Multiply minutes by 60. HIIT clocks and lab protocols share this pair."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:401
msgid "Convert mph to feet per second for ballistics, amusement-ride specs, and US engineering notes that keep length in feet. Multiply mph by 1.46667 (since 88 ft/s = 60 mph). Sports biomechanics in customary units use this."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:383
msgid "Convert mph to km/h when US speed limits, bike computers, or sports radar guns must match metric signage and telemetry. Multiply mph by 1.609344. Touring cyclists and fleet managers localize reports this way."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:431
msgid "Convert mph to m/s for simulations, crash reconstruction inputs, and metric scientific models fed by US speed limits or radar guns. Divide mph by about 2.23694. Automotive research bridging NHTSA and SI tools needs this."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:115
msgid "Convert nanometres to metres in optics, semiconductor process notes, and wavelength tables where light or film thickness is given in nm but equations expect metres (SI base). Physics homework and thin-film coating specs use this constantly. One nanometre is 10⁻⁹ m."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:744
msgid "Convert nm → m by multiplying by 10⁻⁹. Convert nm → µm by dividing by 1 000. Keep powers of ten explicit in lab notebooks. A one-line dimensional check after every conversion catches most transcription mistakes before they enter a paper draft."
msgstr "حوّل nm → m بالضرب في 10⁻⁹. قم بتحويل nm → μm بالقسمة على 1000. احتفظ بقوى العشرة واضحة في دفاتر الملاحظات المعملية. يؤدي فحص الأبعاد المكون من سطر واحد بعد كل تحويل إلى اكتشاف معظم أخطاء النسخ قبل إدخال مسودة ورقية."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1359
msgid "Convert oven settings between Celsius and Fahrenheit, understand fan-assisted adjustments, and keep recipes reliable across regions."
msgstr "يمكنك تحويل إعدادات الفرن بين الدرجة المئوية والفهرنهايت، وفهم التعديلات بمساعدة المروحة، والحفاظ على موثوقية الوصفات عبر المناطق."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2384
msgid "Convert pounds to kilograms or grams before combining with metric volumes. 1 lb ≈ 453.592 g. Kitchen scales that show ounces need the same care: convert oz → g, then apply density."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:975
msgid "Convert regional units to litres (or millilitres) as soon as possible. Work in SI-friendly volume, then convert back to the utensil or legal unit required for output. That round trip through litres is the cheapest insurance against US/UK name collisions."
msgstr "قم بتحويل الوحدات الإقليمية إلى لتر (أو ملليلتر) في أسرع وقت ممكن. اعمل بحجم مناسب SI، ثم قم بالتحويل مرة أخرى إلى الأداة أو الوحدة القانونية المطلوبة للإخراج. تعتبر هذه الرحلة ذهابًا وإيابًا عبر اللترات أرخص تأمين ضد تضارب الأسماء في الولايات المتحدة والمملكة المتحدة."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1418
msgid "Convert road and trail distances between kilometres and miles, read maps from different countries, and pace trips without unit confusion."
msgstr "قم بتحويل مسافات الطرق والمسارات بين الكيلومترات والأميال، وقراءة الخرائط من بلدان مختلفة، وضبط سرعة الرحلات دون ارتباك بين الوحدات."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1300
msgid "Convert room area between square metres and square feet, add waste factor the right way, and avoid the classic length×width unit mix-up."
msgstr "قم بتحويل مساحة الغرفة بين الأمتار المربعة والقدم المربع، وأضف عامل النفايات بالطريقة الصحيحة، وتجنب الخلط بين وحدات الطول × العرض الكلاسيكية."

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:505
msgid "Convert seconds to hours for uptime reports, render-farm jobs, and endurance sports when logs show seconds but humans want hours. Divide seconds by 3,600. Cloud billing dashboards often store seconds underneath."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:445
msgid "Convert seconds to minutes for race results, microwave experiments, and API timeouts when logs show raw seconds. Divide seconds by 60. Sports broadcasting and backend SLAs both humanize seconds this way."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1840
msgid "Convert seconds, minutes, hours, and days without off-by-sixty errors, choose appropriate precision for sports and science, and keep timestamps consistent."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:209
msgid "Convert square centimetres to square inches for US packaging die-lines, bandage sizes, and small panel cutouts when the CAD file is metric. Divide cm² by 6.4516. Print finishers and medical device labeling use this often."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:203
msgid "Convert square inches to square centimetres for packaging labels, gasket cross-sections, and sheet sticker sizes when US print specs meet metric manufacturing. Multiply in² by 6.4516 exactly (since 1 in = 2.54 cm)."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:191
msgid "Convert square kilometres to square miles for country size, wildfire perimeters, and city area comparisons in international news. Geographers and emergency management briefings use both. One square mile is 2.589988110336 km²."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:215
msgid "Convert square metres to hectares for gardens, solar arrays, and small farms when a site survey in m² must match agricultural hectare language. Divide m² by 10,000. Planners jump from building footprints to plot scale with this pair."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:167
msgid "Convert square metres to square feet for apartments, offices, and flooring quotes when the listing is metric but US buyers think in sq ft. Real-estate portals and rug shops use this constantly. Multiply m² by about 10.7639."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:333
msgid "Convert stone to kilograms when a UK weight mention must enter a metric BMI calculator, racing form, or EU medical record. Multiply stone by 6.35029318. Include any extra pounds by converting them to kg and adding."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1604
msgid "Convert the full value you know. If you know stone and pounds, combine them (or convert via kilograms) so leftover pounds are not dropped. Forms that want kg should receive a single kilogram number."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1379
msgid "Convert the printed recipe temperature first, then apply the fan adjustment. Do not mix the steps or you will double-correct."
msgstr "قم بتحويل درجة حرارة الوصفة المطبوعة أولاً، ثم قم بتطبيق ضبط المروحة. لا تخلط الخطوات وإلا فسوف تقوم بالتصحيح المزدوج."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1407
msgid "Convert the printed temperature first, then apply your oven’s recommended fan reduction. Conversion and fan adjustment are separate steps."
msgstr "قم بتحويل درجة الحرارة المطبوعة أولاً، ثم قم بتطبيق تقليل المروحة الموصى به في الفرن. التحويل وتعديل المروحة هما خطوتان منفصلتان."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:465
msgid "Convert to the base SI unit first, then to the destination prefix. That two-step habit prevents tangled mental decimal shifts when you are tired."
msgstr "قم بالتحويل إلى الوحدة الأساسية SI أولاً، ثم إلى بادئة الوجهة. هذه العادة المكونة من خطوتين تمنع التحولات العشرية العقلية المتشابكة عندما تكون متعبًا."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1967
msgid "Convert using Year (Julian) ↔ Day when you need transparent second-based duration. Document the choice in your notebook: “years mean Julian years (365.25 d).”"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:475
msgid "Convert weeks to days for training plans, rental periods, and sprint schedules when coaches or leases say weeks but calendars show days. Multiply weeks by 7. Habit trackers and agile boards use this constantly."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:102
msgid "Convert when you must compare, manufacture, dose, or navigate across systems. If a local building code, speed limit, or packaging label already matches your tools, work in that system and convert only at interfaces—imports, exports, and published specs."
msgstr "قم بالتحويل عندما يتعين عليك المقارنة أو التصنيع أو الجرعة أو التنقل عبر الأنظمة. إذا كان رمز البناء المحلي أو حد السرعة أو ملصق التغليف يتطابق بالفعل مع أدواتك، فاعمل في هذا النظام وقم بالتحويل فقط في الواجهات — عمليات الاستيراد والتصدير والمواصفات المنشورة."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:608
msgid "Converter UIs should separate quantity tabs: Length, Area, Volume, Temperature. Cross-quantity conversion options invite nonsense results. If you build tools, disable impossible pairs."
msgstr "يجب أن تفصل واجهات المستخدم الخاصة بالمحول بين علامات تبويب الكمية: الطول والمساحة والحجم ودرجة الحرارة. خيارات التحويل عبر الكمية تدعو إلى نتائج لا معنى لها. إذا قمت ببناء أدوات، قم بتعطيل الأزواج المستحيلة."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:993
msgid "Converters that expose a single cup unit should document which cup they implement. Users deserve that footnote. If you publish recipe software, store volumes internally in millilitres and localise the display unit—do not store ambiguous cup counts as if they were universal constants."
msgstr "يجب على المحولات التي تعرض وحدة كوب واحدة أن توثق الكوب الذي تستخدمه. يستحق المستخدمون هذه الحاشية السفلية. إذا قمت بنشر برنامج وصفات، قم بتخزين الكميات داخليًا بالملليلتر وقم بإضفاء الطابع المحلي على وحدة العرض - لا تقم بتخزين أعداد الأكواب الغامضة كما لو كانت ثوابت عالمية."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:789
msgid "Converting Acres, Hectares, and Square Metres"
msgstr "تحويل فدان وهكتار ومتر مربع"

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:204
msgid "Converting inches to cm then forgetting to square (×2.54 instead of ×6.4516) understates area by a factor of 2.54. Screen sizes in inches are usually diagonals, not areas—do not convert a “27-inch” monitor as 27 in². Paper “lb” weights are not areas."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1940
msgid "Converting Julian years to days and hours"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:192
msgid "Converting km to miles then forgetting to square the factor (use ÷2.59, not ÷1.61) understates area badly. Lakes and admin boundaries may use different shoreline rules—unit conversion does not fix definition differences. Do not mix nautical miles into land area."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1798
msgid "Converting knots cleanly"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:690
msgid "Converting light-years to kilometres produces enormous integers. Prefer scientific notation in reports. Check that your converter’s light-year matches the Julian-year definition if you need agreement with catalogue values. A mismatch in year definition is tiny compared with cosmic distances for outreach, but it matters when you reconcile two catalogues to many significant figures."
msgstr "تحويل السنوات الضوئية إلى كيلومترات ينتج عنه أعداد صحيحة هائلة. يفضل التدوين العلمي في التقارير. تأكد من أن السنة الضوئية للمحول الخاص بك تتطابق مع تعريف السنة اليوليانية إذا كنت بحاجة إلى اتفاق مع قيم الكتالوج. يعد عدم التطابق في تعريف السنة صغيرًا مقارنة بالمسافات الكونية للتواصل، ولكنه مهم عند التوفيق بين كتالوجين والعديد من الأرقام المهمة."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2465
msgid "Converting metric and US training plans"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/convert/data/conversion-pair-content.ts:80
msgid "Converting only the whole feet and dropping leftover inches loses several centimetres. “Five foot two” must include the two inches (157.5 cm total), not 5 × 30.48 alone. Flooring sold per square foot still needs linear cm for cut lengths—do not mix area and length units."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2157
msgid "Converting stone and pounds to kilograms"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/cookie-consent.tsx:72
msgid "Cookie Consent"
msgstr "موافقة ملفات تعريف الارتباط"

#: src/components/footer.tsx:78
msgid "Cookie settings"
msgstr "إعدادات ملفات تعريف الارتباط"

#: src/routes/$lang/privacy-policy.tsx:128
msgid "Cookies and similar technologies"
msgstr "ملفات تعريف الارتباط والتقنيات المماثلة"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:957
msgid "Cooking consequences"
msgstr "عواقب الطبخ"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:77
msgid "Cooking is the most common place non-engineers hit unit friction. Metric recipes weigh flour and liquids in grams and millilitres; US recipes lean on cups and tablespoons. Weight is more reliable than volume for dry goods because packing density varies. When you must convert volume, treat cup and litre conversions carefully and prefer weighing when accuracy matters."
msgstr "الطبخ هو المكان الأكثر شيوعًا الذي يتعرض فيه غير المهندسين للاحتكاك بالوحدة. الوصفات المترية تزن الدقيق والسوائل بالجرام والمليلتر. الوصفات الأمريكية تعتمد على الكؤوس والملاعق الكبيرة. الوزن أكثر موثوقية من الحجم بالنسبة للبضائع الجافة لأن كثافة التعبئة تختلف. عندما يتعين عليك تحويل الحجم، تعامل مع تحويلات الكوب واللتر بعناية وفضل الوزن عندما تكون الدقة مهمة."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2409
msgid "Cooking syrups: converting a recipe from “grams of honey” to tablespoons requires density (or a tested volumetric equivalent). Guessing from water’s density over-pours honey."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:333
msgid "Cooking Volume Conversions: Cups, Litres, and Spoons"
msgstr "تحويلات حجم الطبخ: الكؤوس، لتر، والملاعق"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:355
msgid "Core volume relationships for the kitchen"
msgstr "علاقات الحجم الأساسية للمطبخ"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1549
msgid "Countries that use metric post body weight and baggage limits in kilograms. US gyms, some airlines’ US-facing pages, and older medical charts still speak in pounds. If you travel, train, or shop across those systems, convert once into a single “home unit,” then keep every note in that unit until you must publish the other."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2033
msgid "Create a line per room: raw L, raw W, unit, net area, waste %, order area, seller unit. Sum order areas. Compare to the installer’s takeoff. Differences larger than a few percent deserve a phone call before payment."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:609
msgid "CSV exports from CAD or GIS tools sometimes drop unit metadata. Re-attach units before converting, and sanity-check magnitudes: a house lot of 500 might be m²; a house lot of 500 000 is probably not acres."
msgstr "أحيانًا تُسقط صادرات ملف CSV من أدوات CAD أو GIS البيانات التعريفية للوحدة. أعد توصيل الوحدات قبل التحويل، وتحقق من سلامة الأبعاد: قد تبلغ مساحة قطعة أرض تبلغ 500 مترًا مربعًا؛ قطعة أرض مساحتها 500000 ربما لا تكون فدانًا."

#: src/lib/units.ts:1241
msgid "Cubic Centimetre"
msgstr "سنتيمتر مكعب"

#: src/lib/units.ts:1240
